SRC/toys -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  pacman.c, 2026-09-26, rebuilt -qm from recipe `pacman'.    - It set stdout unbuffered, and this C library's printf() writes      control bytes in place of its text to an unbuffered stdout -- at a      terminal that was a row of `+' and nothing more.  stdout stays      buffered; the program already called flush() wherever the screen has      to be seen, and two flush() calls were added before the questions it      reads with read() and readln().    - It forked Microware's `tmode nopause noecho', and `tmode normal' to      put the terminal back.  noecho() and echo() now set those two options      with _gs_opt/_ss_opt, and put back the options they found.    - Its cursor addressing was the ADM-3A/TeleVideo ESC = row col, and      its clear screen ESC *.  Both now come from the terminal's termcap      (`cm' and `cl', TERM and TERMCAP as SYS/login sets them).  The original is pacman.c.ori.